 "id": "gather.2",
 "text": "gather.2: the specification declares `trait Tuple extends Any excludes { Object }` (Specification/basic-lib/objects.tex:180-186), but its rule makes every trait except Any and Object implicitly extend Object (Specification/basic/traits.tex:186-188; Specification/basic-lib/objects.tex:159-160). Rung S's desugaring follows the rule and leaves only Any's and Object's own declarations as written (ProjectFortress/src/com/sun/fortress/compiler/desugarer/PreDisambiguationDesugaringVisitor.java:123-124). Neither library declares Tuple, so nothing reaches this today. A library that shipped the specification's Tuple would have it made an Object, against its own excludes clause. Should the rule and the desugaring name Tuple beside Any and Object? There is no default on record. Raised in explorations/compile-ladder/rung-string-conversion/SKEPTIC.md:94 (section 5); Specification/appendices/changes.tex:423 reads \"Object extends Any alone and Tuple likewise\".",
 "inPlan": true
}
